Ultimate Echo Echo can release sonic waves from the [[Sonic Disc|Sonic Discs]] on his body. These sound waves are powerful enough to shatter steel,{{Refn|''[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: Power Struggle]]''; [[:File:PS DVD Ultimate Echo Echo Data.png|file]]|group = DVD|name = DVD}} throw [[Ultimate Kevin]] through several buildings at once,<ref name="AP2" /> heavily damage a [[Petrosapien (Classic)|Petrosapien]],<ref name="TUS">''[[The Ultimate Sacrifice]]''</ref> paralyze an [[Opticoid (Classic)|Opticoid]],<ref name="TUH">''[[The Ultimate Heist]]''</ref> and temporarily contain a blast from a [[Nuclear Fusion Grenade]].<ref name="TEoME">''[[The Enemy of My Enemy]]''</ref>

Ultimate Echo Echo can create force fields out of sonic waves that are strong enough to block Petrosapien crystal shards.<ref name="AP2" /> Ultimate Echo Echo can also release sonic screams like his [[Echo Echo|devolved form]], as demonstrated by his [[Sentient Ultimate Echo Echo|sentient counterpart]].<ref name="TUH" />

Ultimate Echo Echo can fly and levitate by using sound waves.<ref name="MoI">''[[Map of Infinity (Episode)|Map of Infinity]]''</ref><ref>''[[Viktor: The Spoils]]''</ref>{{Refn|group = DVD|name = DVD}}

Ultimate Echo Echo possesses enhanced strength, enough to briefly help [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] hold open a door in the temple on [[Mikd'lty]].<ref name="MoI" />

Ultimate Echo Echo is durable enough to withstand being thrown through the walls of [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s [[Ben's House|house]]<ref name="TPG">''[[The Perfect Girlfriend]]''</ref> and getting smacked by a [[To'kustar (Classic)|To'kustar]], as demonstrated by his sentient counterpart.<ref name="TUS"/>

Ultimate Echo Echo can survive and use his powers in the vacuum of space.<ref name="TEoME" />

Ultimate Echo Echo is immune to low temperatures, like those on Mikd'lty.<ref name="MoI" />

===Equipment===
Ultimate Echo Echo can send out the [[Sonic Disc]]s on his body to project powerful sonic blasts, which can easily knock out his opponents, destroy projectiles or even a military tank.<ref name="AP2" /> Ultimate Echo Echo can also multiply the Sonic Discs once they have separated from his body, creating as many as needed.<ref name="AP2" />

Ultimate Echo Echo can use his Sonic Discs to use an exceedingly deadly move called Sonic Doom, where his discs surround the enemy and fire full sonic blasts. This move was powerful enough to subdue [[Ultimate Kevin]].<ref name="AP2" /> 

Ultimate Echo Echo's Sonic Discs can continue flying and attacking even after he transforms back to normal.<ref name="GfT">''[[Greetings From Techadon]]''</ref>

Ultimate Echo Echo's Sonic Discs can capture/reproduce sound waves out of phase, thus canceling out the sound in the environment.{{Refn|[[:File:Ultimate Echo Echo Can Cancel Sound Waves.png]]|group = CM}}

===Non-Canon Powers and Abilities===
====Cartoon Network Action Pack!====
If multiple [[Echo Echo]] clones press the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] to transform into Ultimate Echo Echo at the same time, all of the Echo Echo clones will become Ultimate Echo Echo clones.{{Refn|''[[Fashion Victim]]''|group = AP}}

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
TUH (509).png|Shared Pain/Electricity Vulnerability
AP2 (474).png|Magnetism Vulnerability
TPG (441).png|Suffocation
</gallery>
Like his [[Echo Echo|devolved form]], Ultimate Echo Echo is vulnerable to electricity, such as that generated by a [[Gimlinopithecus]].<ref name="TUH" /> Ultimate Echo Echo also will feel pain if his [[Sonic Disc]]s are damaged, demonstrated when they were electrocuted.<ref name="TUH" />

Ultimate Echo Echo's skin is somewhat metallic, which means he can be easily magnetized by a [[Biotsavartian]].<ref name="AP2" />

Ultimate Echo Echo can be suffocated if a large amount of matter enters his lungs.<ref name="TPG" />

Like his devolved form, Ultimate Echo Echo can also unintentionally hurt his teammates' ears with his sonic vibrations, as demonstrated with his [[Sentient Ultimate Echo Echo|sentient counterpart]].<ref name="TUS" />

Unlike his devolved form, Ultimate Echo Echo does not have the ability to duplicate himself.{{Refn|
Various statements made by the crew offer contradictory accounts whether Ultimate Echo Echo retains his devolved counterpart's self-duplication abilities.
*During '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]'''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s run, a bio for Ultimate Echo Echo featured on [[Cartoon Network]]'s website stated that Ultimate Echo Echo could self-duplicate.{{Refn|[[:File:Cartoonnetwork Info Ultiamte Echo Echo.png]]|group = CN}} However, [[Dwayne McDuffie]] stated that Ultimate Echo Echo did not possess this ability.{{Refn|[[:File:UEE Cannot Duplicate.PNG]]|group = DM}}
*Derrick J. Wyatt thought that Ultimate Echo Echo's [[Sonic Disc]]s could detach from him and then a body would drop down from the disc so he could duplicate by transforming rather than copying. This is why he redesigned Ultimate Echo Echo's discs in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''' to resemble his head, only to later find out he could not duplicate.{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick's Opinion on the Ultimates' Designs.png]]|group = DJW}}
**In Derrick's opinion, Ultimate Echo Echo can duplicate in '''Omniverse'''{{Refn|[[:File:Ultimate Echo Echo Can Duplicate in OV.png]]|group = DJW}} despite not displaying the power on-screen.{{Refn|[[:File:Ultimate Echo Echo Can Duplicate in OV 2.png]]|group = DJW}} He also explained his inability to do so in '''Ultimate Alien''' as being due to a glitch with the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]].{{Refn|[[:File:Ultimate Echo Echo Inability to Duplicate Glitch.png]]|group = DJW}}|group = note}}

==History==
===Ultimate Alien===
*Ultimate Echo Echo first appeared in ''[[Map of Infinity (Episode)|Map of Infinity]]'', where he defeated some [[Necrofriggian]]s and explored the temple on [[Mikd'lty]], during which he defeated [[Cerberus]]. He eventually switched into [[Four Arms (Classic)|Four Arms]] to help [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] hold a door open.
*In ''[[The Enemy of My Enemy]]'', Ultimate Echo Echo saved the [[Plumbers' Academy|Plumber's Academy]] from a [[Nuclear Fusion Grenade|nuclear bomb]].
*In ''[[Absolute Power: Part 2]]'', Ultimate Echo Echo defeated [[Ultimate Kevin]] and prepared to finish him off before [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] convinced him otherwise.
*In ''[[Viktor: The Spoils]]'', Ultimate Echo Echo saved the [[Rustbucket 3]] from some missiles.
*In ''[[Basic Training]]'', Ultimate Echo Echo briefly appeared at the beginning after battling [[Trombipulor]].
*In ''[[Greetings From Techadon]]'', Ultimate Echo Echo battled a silver [[Techadon Robot]] and figured out how to stop it.
*In ''[[Double or Nothing]]'', Ultimate Echo Echo defeated [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Rath (Classic)|Rath]].
*In ''[[The Perfect Girlfriend]]'', Ultimate Echo Echo fought [[Elena Valadis|Elena]] who nearly suffocated him to death with her [[Microchip]]s until [[Julie Yamamoto|Julie]] convinced her to spare him.
*In ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', Ultimate Echo Echo was seen confronting [[Albedo]] in a dream.

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[The Ultimate Heist]]'', Negative Ultimate Echo Echo defeated [[Eye Guy]], but was defeated by [[Shocksquatch]] and switched into Negative [[Ultimate Spidermonkey]].
*In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', Negative Ultimate Echo Echo chased an Omnitrixless [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Prime]] only to be sent back to the Prime Timeline by [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] as [[Clockwork]].

